# WINARM (P5, sprint_p05_detail.md D5 row 2): the win_io twin of the POSIX
# file-I/O slice — UCRT _open/_creat/_read/_write/_close via the resolver's
# underscore alias. Loads everywhere (FFI pragmas resolve at call time);
# RUNS only on Windows (the platformName guard in 99_run_all.mst).
59_win_io_tests.mst
# WINARM (WG0, docs/sprints/sprint_wg0_detail.md): the Windows GUI world
# LAYER, loaded from here — the one place outside world/winui.list that
# names it, and not by choice. The probe classes deliberately stay out of
# world.list (the base world must remain byte-identical), but an unresolved
# capitalised name in a method body is a COMPILE error in this dialect and
# the guest has no dynamic `Smalltalk at:` to reach a global with, so
# 60_winui_probe_tests.mst cannot load at all unless its layer loaded
# first. `..` resolves against world/tests/, i.e. world/90_winui_probe.mst;
# both `it_world.rs::load_tests_list` and the justfile's concatenating
# differential gates handle it identically. The layer is inert off Windows
# (FFI pragmas resolve at CALL time) and its tests are platformName-guarded
# in 99_run_all.mst.
../90_winui_probe.mst
60_winui_probe_tests.mst
99_run_all.mst
